Now, there are some cases where you might want to have the **same schema for input and output**. Probably the main use case for this is if you already have some autogenerated client code/SDKs and you don't want to update all the autogenerated client code/SDKs yet, you probably will want to do it at some point, but maybe not right now. In that case, you can disable this feature in **FastAPI** , with the parameter `separate_input_output_schemas=False`. Note Support for `separate_input_output_schemas` was added in FastAPI `0.102.0`. 🤓 Python 3.10+

