But if you go to the browser at http://127.0.0.1:8000/items/foo, you will see a nice HTTP error of:

```json
{
  "detail": [
    {
      "type": "int_parsing",
      "loc": [
        "path",
        "item_id"
      ],
      "msg": "Input should be a valid integer, unable to parse string as an integer",
      "input": "foo"
    }
  ]
}
```

because the path parameter `item_id` had a value of `"foo"`, which is not an `int`. The same error would appear if you provided a `float` instead of an `int`, as in: http://127.0.0.1:8000/items/4.2 Tip So, with the same Python type declaration, **FastAPI** gives you data validation. Notice that the error also clearly states exactly the point where the validation didn't pass. This is incredibly helpful while developing and debugging code that interacts with your API.

